{
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "notes": "Real hardware run of modem_cfun_test.py confirmed AT+CFUN=0 -> AT+CFUN=1 works end to end (stayed UART-responsive, re-registered successfully). Wired it into the real automatic logging flow: Sim7600Modem.close_data() now sends AT+CFUN=0 after HTTPTERM/NETCLOSE, cutting the modem's RF/network draw between cycles -- ensure_data()'s existing self.reset() (a hardware reset, called at the start of every cycle regardless) already reliably wakes it, unchanged, so this adds a real power-saving step with no new wake-up risk. Also fixed a real pre-existing bug the same hardware run's transient '+CME ERROR: SIM busy' response almost hit: check_sim()'s error paths called an undefined _one_line() (should be one_line(), no underscore) -- would have raised a confusing NameError instead of a clear CellularError the moment either branch was ever actually hit. Never caught before because the SIM always answered READY immediately in every prior test. check_sim() now also retries briefly on that exact 'SIM busy' transient (confirmed to happen right after AT+CFUN=1 while the SIM reinitializes) instead of failing immediately. auto_log.py's INTERVAL_ENGINE_OFF_S is temporarily set to 5 minutes (matching the engine-on interval) for a multi-day standalone battery-life test -- revert to 60 minutes for real field/dock use once that test is done.",
